From 0d274077c977fd4a93f39d723a58504570d635fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:42:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(linux): build the Linux AppImage in a reproducible
 container

Add docker/Dockerfile and docker/Makefile defining the Linux build
environment (the build-linux apt packages plus SDL2/tinyxml2/libzip built
from source, frozen into image layers), and rewire the build-linux job to
produce its AppImage with `make -C docker appimage`.

The container mirrors the job's environment exactly; the only intended
change is freezing the floating `ubuntu-latest` runner and the from-source
library steps into image layers, so the build is reproducible and a
developer can run the identical build locally with `make -C docker appimage`.
The generate-port-o2r job and the uploaded artifact are unchanged: the job
still downloads ghostship.o2r (now to the repo root, where the build bundles
it) and uploads the same files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
